src/

	-- Contains the implementation of the assembler components.

	main.c — Controls the overall assembler flow.
	lexer.c — Reads the source file and identifies lines, instructions, and operands.
	instruction.c — Classifies operands based on their type.
	register.c — Loads and searches register definitions.
	opcode.c — Loads and searches instruction definitions.

include/
	-- Contains header files with structures, enums, and 
	   function declarations used by the source files.

	lexer.h
	instruction.h
	register.h
	opcode.h

data/
	-- Contains architecture and assembler definition data 
	   instead of hard-coding it in C.

	registers.txt — Supported IA-32 registers and their encoding values.
	opcode.txt — Instructions currently supported by the assembler.

examples/
	-- Contains sample .asm programs used for manual testing.

tests/
	-- Contains test cases for checking individual assembler 
	   components and overall behavior.
Development Stages
Stage 1 — Source Reading
	-- Read the complete assembly file into a memory buffer.

Stage 2 — Line Detection
	-- Introduced lineT to track the starting position 
		and length of each source line.

Stage 3 — Content Detection
	-- Introduced contentT to track the line number and 
	   beginning of meaningful content.

Stage 4 — Instruction Detection
	-- Introduced instructionT to locate the instruction/mnemonic in each line.

Stage 5 — Operand Detection
	-- Introduced operandT to locate each operand using its start and len.

Stage 6 — Operand Classification
	-- Introduced Operand and OperandType to 
	   classify operands as register, immediate, memory, etc.

Stage 7 — Data-Driven Definitions
	-- Moved register and instruction definitions into data/ files 
	   so they can be loaded and searched instead of being hard-coded.
